# Normalise line endings so a Windows clone and a macOS/Linux clone have the
# SAME BYTES in the working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) rewrites
# text files to CRLF on checkout. That is invisible to `git diff` — git
# normalises on the way back in — so the tree looks clean while the bytes on
# disk differ from every other platform. It silently broke a writer test that
# asserted on a literal "\n", for a reason that had nothing to do with the code
# under test. Pinning eol=lf keeps the checkout identical everywhere.
#
# The allowlist writer separately preserves whatever endings the OPERATOR's own
# config arrived with (Notepad writes CRLF); that is a runtime property and is
# unaffected by this file.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch, never diff as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.mp4    binary
*.webm   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ico    binary
